      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled dose of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Each 1,700 mg dose also exceeds the usual maximum single dose of about 1,000 mg (850 mg is a common upper dose with meals). At this level there is a serious risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals**\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I would still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
